  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Version:\nEarliest known occurrence: 2018.4.3p1\nMost recent occurrence: 2019.2.1\n\nDescription of the bug:\nSometimes when in desktop, I will find that looking in a specific direction in a world will cause a portion of the screen to flicker between what I expect to see and what I can only describe as another viewpoint of the world.\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\nSo far I've only had or seen the issue occur in desktop. I have tried going back to the same worlds where the issue has happened but have never been able to successfully reproduce the issue. I play many hours a week in VR and have not had this issue once while in VR. The issue only rarely occurs when I play in desktop mode which I don't do very often.\n\nThe only hardware in common between myself and a streamer I have seen also have this issue is that we both have EVGA GTX 1070 Ti 8GB graphics cards\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\nI have saved a few of clips of a twitch streamer that also sometimes experiences this issue:\nhttps://clips.twitch.tv/BlightedTubularPigNotLikeThis (February 6th 2019)\nhttps://clips.twitch.tv/CulturedHilariousMinkBleedPurple (March 12th 2019)\nhttps://clips.twitch.tv/JollyKawaiiTubersAliens (March 12th 2019)\nAttached are screenshots taken by myself standing completely still on December 16th 2018, my screen was constantly flickering between the two screenshots.",
